//! The `baseline-shift` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property repositions
//! the dominant-baseline of a text element relative to the dominant-baseline of its parent text
//! content element. The shifted element might be a sub- or superscript. If the property is present,
//! the value overrides the element's `baseline-shift` attribute.
//!
//! Initial: 0. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: refer to the used value of `line-height`.
//!
//! Grammar: <length-percentage> | sub | super | top | center | bottom
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-inline-3/#propdef-baseline-shift
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/baseline-shift
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

